/-!
# Arithmetic Harmonic Analysis at the Spacing Scale

Umbrella for the harmonic analysis of Weil's form on the atomic family
`f_x = Σ_{n ≤ N} x_n g(· − log n)` at the spacing `δ_N = log(1 + 1/N)` of the atoms: the
self-energy of an atom with constant one, the archimedean cross kernel, the tilted Schur rows of
the prime form, and the stability law at the spacing scale with its gauge blindness; the
diamagnetic inequality (`ζ` is the ground state of its gauge orbit); and the law that positivity on
the atomic families of one fixed bump — unbounded overlap — is the Riemann hypothesis.
See `SpacingScaleHarmonicAnalysis/README.md`.
-/
